@echo off
cd /d "C:\Users\SubratoBiswas\trinamix-conversion-workbench"
echo Cleaning any git locks...
del /f /q ".git\index.lock" 2>nul
del /f /q ".git\HEAD.lock" 2>nul
echo Dropping tracked bytecode...
git rm -r --cached --ignore-unmatch backend/app/__pycache__ backend/app/services/__pycache__ backend/app/parsers/__pycache__
echo Staging...
git add -A
echo Committing (no-op if clean)...
git commit -m "Fix FBDI bundle timeout on multi-sheet objects (Customer/Item). The row transform was already chunked + threaded like supplier, but the OUTPUT WRITE wasn't: generate_output_artifact always wrote xlsx via openpyxl, even when the bundle asked for CSV. Measured: xlsx of 2 sheets x 5599 rows = 8s, so a 19-sheet Customer load ~= 77s > the 60s request limit = 'Could not build the FBDI bundle'. Two fixes. (1) Honor fmt=csv: multi-sheet objects now write one CSV per interface table into a .zip (which is also the correct format for an actual Fusion FBDI load), single-sheet objects a plain .csv; the whole write runs in a worker thread so it never blocks the event loop. Measured new path: all 19 sheets x 5599 rows in 0.56s (~130x faster). XLSX is kept for explicit single-file xlsx downloads. (2) The bundle endpoint no longer runs full AI mapping inline for every conversion - that was a second 60s sink; generate_output_artifact already force-applies the learned standards, so the bundle just generates + zips. Structure/linkage pass verified unchanged (0.02s)."
echo Pushing...
git push origin main
echo.
echo ====== DONE - Press any key to close ======
pause
